# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kynovant Staging — env contract template
#
# Copy this file to `.env.staging.local` (gitignored — never commit the
# real one) and fill in the values from the EXISTING "Kynovant Staging"
# Supabase project. Do not create a new staging project — one already
# exists; see docs/staging-environment.md for its identifiers
# (project ref, region, org) and setup history.
#
# Get every value below from the Supabase dashboard for that project —
# Settings → API (URL, publishable/anon key, service role key) and
# Settings → Database (connection strings) — never from Vercel's env
# store, which only holds PRODUCTION's values under these same names.
#
# After filling this in, verify it before running anything against it:
#   set -a && source .env.staging.local && set +a
#   npx tsx scripts/assert-staging-db.ts
#
# npm run test:staging does the source + verify + test run for you.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Pooled connection — what the app runtime (getDb() in lib/db/client.ts)
# uses. From Supabase → Settings → Database → Connection string →
# "Transaction" pooler mode.
DATABASE_URL=

# Direct (non-pooled) connection — required specifically for running
# migrations (scripts/migrate.ts). From Supabase → Settings → Database
# → Connection string → "Session" / direct mode.
DATABASE_URL_DIRECT=

# From Supabase → Settings → API → Project URL.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# From Supabase → Settings → API → Project API keys → anon/publishable.
# Matches lib/supabase/client.ts's NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY —
# this repo's name for what Supabase's dashboard may still label "anon".
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# From Supabase → Settings → API → Project API keys → service_role.
# Never expose this to a client bundle — server-only, matches
# lib/supabase/admin.ts.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional — only needed for AI-provider-backed generator work
# (day-generation benchmarking, real staging program runs), not for
# plain DB-backed tests. Per docs/staging-environment.md's fixture
# policy, no other production secret (Stripe, Resend, Calendly, Sheets,
# DocuSign) belongs in this file — DB-backed/generator test work never
# needs them, and copying them here would widen this file's blast
# radius for no benefit.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Model identifier passed to the Vercel AI Gateway (see
# lib/program-generator/provider.ts). Safe to reuse production's value
# here — it's a model name, not a credential — but keep AI Gateway
# usage attributable: prefer a distinct API key/project scope if your
# AI Gateway setup supports it, so staging benchmark spend is visible
# separately from production spend.
# PROGRAM_GENERATOR_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4
